From: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: qcom: invalidate MSM8226 context TLB on reset

MSM8226 BSP __reset_context() invalidates the context TLB before
installing new TTBRs. The current helper omits this operation. In a kexec
boot this can retain entries/table-walk state from the preceding display.

Match the exact BSP context-local TLBIALL while the bank is disabled and
the instance front-end halted. The unhalt barrier completes these writes
before client requests resume. Do not touch secure global invalidation
registers or change the existing long-descriptor instances.

Related upstream fix by Sam Day, checked2026-10-14 (v1, not in this base):
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260928-qcom-iommu-clean-contexts-v1-1-c88fe2b4ff48@samcday.com
Link: https://github.com/LineageOS/android_kernel_samsung_msm8226/blob/3fa1853ed5d6c3a8ef5a2fda9822705243bbc256/drivers/iommu/msm_iommu-v1.c

Signed-off-by: BlackF1re <55582873+BlackF1re@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
index 203c0a925..f2632f43a 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu/qcom_iommu.c
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@
 #define SMMU_INTR_SEL_NS     0x2000
 #define MICRO_MMU_CTRL_HALT_REQ BIT(2)
 #define MICRO_MMU_CTRL_IDLE BIT(3)
+#define QCOM_IOMMU_CB_TLBIALL 0x618
 
 enum qcom_iommu_clk {
 	CLK_IFACE,
@@ -302,6 +303,10 @@ static int qcom_iommu_program_ctx(struct qcom_iommu_dev *qcom_iommu,
 	/* Disable context bank before programming */
 	iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_SCTLR, 0);
 
+	/* Match the MSM8226 BSP reset: discard stale firmware translations. */
+	if (qcom_iommu->short_desc)
+		iommu_writel(ctx, QCOM_IOMMU_CB_TLBIALL, 0);
+
 	/* Clear context bank fault address fault status registers */
 	iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_FAR, 0);
 	iommu_writel(ctx, ARM_SMMU_CB_FSR, ARM_SMMU_CB_FSR_FAULT);
